# Code Style

Nun = Discord client mod (TypeScript + React + webpack patches, Vencord/Equicord fork).
Prioritize correctness, minimal code, and existing utilities. No overengineering.

---

# Core Principles

- Minimal change > refactor
- Declarative APIs > manual wiring
- Prefer existing utilities over custom code
- No comments unless explicitly requested
- No unused abstractions or defensive coding
- Keep code small, direct, predictable

---

# Plugin Structure

```ts
import definePlugin from "@utils/types";

export default definePlugin({
  name: "Plugin",
  description: "Plugin description",
});
```

Use declarative APIs:
- `flux` over FluxDispatcher subscriptions
- `contextMenus` over manual patches
- `chatBarButton` / `messagePopoverButton` over manual UI injection
- `managedStyle` over manual style toggles

Lifecycle:
- Everything in `start()` must be cleaned in `stop()` unless declarative API handles it

---

# Forbidden Patterns

| Bad | Good |
|---|---|
| `value !== null && value !== undefined` | `value != null` |
| `array && array.length > 0` | `array?.length` |
| `value \|\| default` | `value ?? default` |
| template concat | `classes()` |
| hardcoded CDN URLs | `IconUtils.*` |
| `/api/v9/...` | `Constants.Endpoints` |
| `any` | typed Discord objects |
| `as unknown as` | correct typing |
| `React.memo()` | remove |
| `React.cloneElement` | alternative approach |
| `React.lazy(import())` | `LazyComponent` |
| empty `catch {}` | handled error |
| `console.log/warn` | remove |
| `document.querySelector` | webpack patches |
| magic numbers | constants |
| commented dead code | delete |

---

# TypeScript Rules

- Prefer inference
- Use `const`, arrow functions
- Early returns > nesting
- No redundant types
- No comments

---

# React Rules

- Return `null` only (never undefined)
- Always cleanup effects
- Wrap patched components in ErrorBoundary
- Use proper cleanup for listeners/timers

---

# Discord Types

Always use:

```ts
import { User, Guild, Message } from "@vencord/discord-types";
```

No `any`, no unsafe casts.

---

# CSS

- Always use `classNameFactory`
- Combine via `classes()`

```ts
const cl = classNameFactory("vc-plugin-");
className={classes(cl("x"), cond && cl("y"))}
```

---

# Settings

- `settings.store` = reactive
- `settings.plain` = avoid unless required

---

# Patches

Rules:
- One concern per patch
- Small regex scope (`.{0,n}` only)
- Avoid broad matchers (`.*`)
- Never rely on minified variable names
- Use stable anchors (`#{intl::KEY}`)
- Only capture groups when reused

---

# Plugins Interop

```ts
import { isPluginEnabled } from "@api/PluginManager";

if (!isPluginEnabled(other.name)) return;
```

No direct global plugin access.

---

# Performance

- Map/Set > arrays for lookup
- `.find()` > `.filter()[0]`
- `Promise.all()` for parallel work
- No unnecessary helpers

---

# Cleanup Rules

Every resource must be cleaned unless declarative:
- listeners
- intervals
- observers
- timers
- subscriptions

Prefer declarative APIs to avoid manual cleanup.

---

# Code Hygiene

- Remove dead code
- No overengineering
- No unused imports
- No logging in production plugins
- Prefer fewer lines over abstractions

---

# Built-in Utilities

Do NOT reimplement:

- `@utils/misc`: classes, sleep, parseUrl
- `@utils/css`: classNameFactory
- `@utils/discord`: sendMessage, copyWithToast
- `@utils/react`: hooks
- `@webpack/common`: stores, actions, utils

---

# AI Slop Heuristics

Flag:
- excessive comments
- over-defensive null checks
- unnecessary wrappers
- duplicated utilities
- verbose naming

Still fully review code.

---

# Review Policy

- Focus on real issues only
- Prefer fewer, high-impact findings
- Ignore cosmetic noise
